INTERLIS 2.4;

!! Extension of StandardSymbology (same mechanism as the scale-visibility prototype of interlis-runtime): a text made of two values.
!! The DMAV display rule 'Nummer mit Teilgrundstueck' is Grundstueck.Nummer & "." & Liegenschaft.NummerTeilgrundstueck; INTERLIS has no
!! text concatenation (the scanner rejects '&'), so the sign interface gets the pieces: Txt, then Separator and Suffix when Suffix is defined.
SYMBOLOGY MODEL StandardSymbologyText (en)
  AT "https://example.org/dmavsym/" VERSION "2026-10-22" =

  IMPORTS StandardSymbology;

  TOPIC TextSigns EXTENDS StandardSymbology.StandardSigns =

    CLASS TextSign (EXTENDED) =
    PARAMETER
      Separator : TEXT*10;   !! written between Txt and Suffix
      Suffix    : TEXT;      !! second part of the text; none: the text is Txt alone
    END TextSign;

  END TextSigns;

END StandardSymbologyText.
